WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.760
The Implement phase is about putting the course into use.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.786
It includes publishing format decisions, LMS upload and configuration, learner access,

00:00:07.786 --> 00:00:11.081
launch testing, completion tracking, rollout communication, and support planning.

00:00:11.081 --> 00:00:13.643
Implementation is more than exporting a package.

00:00:13.643 --> 00:00:18.035
It is the operational work that ensures learners can actually launch, complete,

00:00:18.035 --> 00:00:20.231
and be credited for the course.

00:00:20.231 --> 00:00:22.793
Publishing format depends on the delivery environment.

00:00:22.793 --> 00:00:27.918
A SCORM package is commonly used when a course needs to communicate launch, progress,

00:00:27.918 --> 00:00:30.846
completion, score, or interaction data to an LMS.

00:00:30.846 --> 00:00:35.238
Other formats may be used for web delivery, internal portals, blended programs,

00:00:35.238 --> 00:00:36.336
or informal learning.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:40.363
The format should match the tracking and access requirements identified earlier.

00:00:40.363 --> 00:00:42.925
LMS configuration should be tested before launch.

00:00:42.925 --> 00:00:47.317
Confirm the course opens correctly, resumes as expected if resume is required,

00:00:47.317 --> 00:00:49.513
tracks completion, reports score if applicable,

00:00:49.513 --> 00:00:52.441
and behaves correctly for failed or passed assessments.

00:00:52.441 --> 00:00:56.834
Do not assume a package that works locally will behave the same

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.664
way in the target LMS.

00:00:58.664 --> 00:01:01.226
Launch testing is part of implementation quality.

00:01:01.226 --> 00:01:02.690
Implementation also includes communication.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:07.448
Learners may need to know why the course matters, how long it takes,

00:01:07.448 --> 00:01:12.207
when it is due, how completion is tracked, and where to get help.

00:01:12.207 --> 00:01:14.037
Managers may need reporting expectations.

00:01:14.037 --> 00:01:18.429
Support teams may need answers for access problems, audio issues, browser questions,

00:01:18.429 --> 00:01:19.527
or completion discrepancies.

00:01:19.527 --> 00:01:21.357
Pilot groups can reduce risk.

00:01:21.357 --> 00:01:25.383
A small rollout can reveal confusing instructions, device issues, LMS behavior,

00:01:25.383 --> 00:01:29.776
missing support information, or content that does not land with the audience.

00:01:29.776 --> 00:01:34.900
Implementation succeeds when the course reaches learners reliably and the surrounding operation supports completion.
